# kills: cancelling an armed DELETE re-syncs the box, GENERATE and the message (queue row 91)
# suite: node --test --test-name-pattern ^cancelling.an.armed.DELETE.re.syncs.the.box..GENERATE.and.the.message..queue.row.91.$ tests/e2e.test.js
# Arming DELETE writes its confirmation into the seed's own row instead of
# #scale-del-note, which is exactly the shape of queue row 91: the parser's
# refusal is overwritten by a message about a different control, and the box
# stays red for a reason the page no longer gives.
# This is the mutant that replaced d_disarm_skips_the_resync. That one mutated
# the disarm's re-derive, and the split made it unobservable - nothing damages
# the seed row any more, so there is nothing for the re-derive to repair. The
# damage has to be reintroduced to be seen, and it has to be READ while DELETE
# is still armed, because the disarm re-derives and would repair it first.
# Re-anchored 2026-10-13 (seeded SAVE / DELETE, lane app) against the current source. The mutation itself is unchanged.
